  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center IOR Underwater Challenges Workshop 01-22 (Virtual)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Near East South Asia Center for Strategic Studies Maritime Workshops cover a variety of topics. Roughly two-thirds of these participants will come from the Indian Ocean littoral countries and the remaining one-third will hail from non-Indian Ocean littoral states with a long tradition of Maritime operations. The programs are designed to be a strategic workshop that foster discussions on areas of littoral security cooperation in the Indian Ocean. The importance of the Indian Ocean is now clear to all interested parties, but there remains a lack of forums wherein conversations on strategy and modified threat response occur. The purpose of NESA Center programs is to encourage informal and constructive dialogue among national security professionals of differing backgrounds and perspectives with the goal of generating ideas and suggestions for cooperative problem solving. To that end, all discussions within the seminars are unofficial in nature, strictly off the record and not for attribution.</narrative>
  </description>
